<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian crude output seen at 2.04 mln bpd in '97.</title>
<headline>Nigerian crude output seen at 2.04 mln bpd in '97.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's crude oil production in 1997 is estimated at around 2.04 million barrels per day (bpd), finance minister Anthony Ani said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Nigeria has an OPEC quota of 1.865 million bpd. A Reuter survey pegged the country's production at 2.06 million bpd in December.</p>
<p>Ani gave the estimate for 1997 production when giving a detailed breakdown of this year's budget.</p>
</text>
